35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Yikes! It looks like we're totally stuck when it comes to finding field staff. We have the experts on the bench, but the partners are way too busy with software!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings suggest that our ""wins"" were actually quite boring, stable tools. The failure came from high-overhead, labor-heavy operations.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"Well, here's the punchline: our credit line is useless for software-as-a-service. It only likes physical assets. And our holdings are eating our reserves way faster than we planned.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found it! The reason we're so stressed is because the software companies just tell us their numbers, but the hardware ones have real things we can check!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My data confirms a pattern. If the company deals with regulated data or physical hardware, the deployment delay is massive. We're signing up for months of silence.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Mizuki, that's exactly what I'm afraid of! If it takes months to deploy and we can't find the people to run it, we're just throwing money into a hole!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,George,,"I'm seeing a clear divide. The software tools with high retention are the real winners, but the labor-intensive models are where we lose our shirts.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly, George! But remember, if we go all-in on software, we can't borrow against it. We'll be relying entirely on our dwindling cash reserves.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"But the software ones make the quarter-end so confusing! I want something we can actually see and touch, as long as it doesn't make the audit take forever!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, ""seeing and touching"" is exactly what causes the delays. The delivery records show that hardware shortages and security reviews are the real killers.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,I can't support anything that requires a massive hiring spree for field crews. We just don't have the recruiter reach for that right now.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,George,,I'm inclined to avoid anything with high operational overhead. The data shows that the simplest models—the ones that just solve a boring problem—are the most resilient.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"I'm torn. I want the stability of software, but I'm terrified of our liquidity. If we invest in a ""boring"" software company, we have no safety net if they need more cash.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't like the ""trust me"" numbers from software companies. But I also don't like the six-week audit delay for hardware! Is there something in the middle?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"There is no middle ground when it comes to deployment. You either have a software tool that deploys in weeks, or a complex system that takes a year.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
